That transcript was a full `initialize` -> `thread/start` -> `turn/start` round trip driven
by `appserver_probe.py` against the same loopback fake standing in for the OpenAI Responses
wire this README's "Fixture provenance" section describes, for a plain
`echo hello` command that never needed to escalate past the sandbox (no
`item/commandExecution/requestApproval` line appears in it at all — see
`app-server-approval.txt` for the escalating case, captured separately). This fixture holds
its last `thread/tokenUsage/updated` notification (`tokenUsage.total.inputTokens: 57`,
`outputTokens: 10`) and its terminal `turn/completed` line, kept verbatim; neither line
carries a scratch path, so there was nothing to rewrite to `/capture`.
